'''Gigahaniwan''' (大型土器ダイハニワン, ''Ōgata Doki Daihaniwan'', '''Colossal Earthenware Daihaniwan''') is a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] variant of [[Haniwanwan]] that appears in [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!]]. It was added in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Gigahaniwan
|image = E 683.png
|first appearance = [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!]]
|money drop = 2,300¢ - 9,085¢
}}

==Enemy==
Similar to its original counterpart, Gigahaniwan boasts a massive amount of HP (that is exacerbated by the scaling buffs from its [[Gauntlet]]), does not get knocked back until death, and can inflict a variety of debuffs which have a higher individual chance of 30% (100% chance for Curse) and longer duration of 3 seconds. Its attack power is lower than a normal Haniwanwan's even in [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!/Excavation Lv.1~20#Excavation Lv.11~20|Excavation Lv.MAX]], but this is mitigated by its 350 range Area Attacks that generate level 4 [[Wave Attack]]s. Additionally, Gigahaniwan's abilities cannot be disabled by [[Curse]], making it all the more difficult to deal with unless the units you are using are immune to its plethora of different debuffs it can inflict.

==Strategy==
In [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!/Excavation Lv.1~20#Excavation Lv.11~20|Excavation Lv.11~20]], Gigahaniwan is supported by [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]]s, making [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] risky to use unless most of your army is immune/resistant to [[Surge Attack|Surges]]. Its Curse Immunity means the likes of [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]] won't be able to prevent it from abusing status effects, but its lack of other Immunities can greatly hinder its ability to push if they come into play. Gigahaniwanwan's surprisingly high range allows it to deny the majority of ranged Wave Shields, and the presence of Golem Sunfish means the use of [[Mighty Kristul Muu (Legend Rare Cat)|Mighty Kristul Muu]] is not advisable due to its low speed, despite it outranging Gigahaniwanwan.

[[True Form]] [[Uncanny Legends]] drop units such as [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]], [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] are incredibly helpful with their anti-Relic abilities, with most of them also packing Colossus Slayer. The aforementioned [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] will also be of great help. Unfortunately, Luza's and Uril's lack of [[Wave Attack|Wave]] immunity will eventually chip them down, Naala does not outrange, and Uril's duplicated Surges can unnecessarily complicate things, but they can still help to ease the fight.

[[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Kenshin]] will be of great help with the Knockback and Immune to Curse [[Talents]], though she may struggle as the battle drags on.

